Here is a complete UI implementation designed to display and filter your eight-item list. 

First, we send the `createSurface` message to initialize the UI canvas:

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9.1",
  "createSurface": {
    "surfaceId": "task-tracker-surface",
    "catalogId": "https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/c-data-display.json"
  }
}
</a2ui-json>

Next, we send the `updateComponents` message to construct the layout. This UI utilizes:
1. A **Heading** and **Body** introduction to orient the user.
2. A **Metric Row** summarizing status distribution.
3. A **Chip Group** serving as the interactive status filter bar.
4. A **Sortable Data Table** clearly presenting the eight items with their title, status indicator, and one-line detail.

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9.1",
  "updateComponents": {
    "surfaceId": "task-tracker-surface",
    "components": [
      {
        "id": "root",
        "component": "heading",
        "text": "Project Deliverables Board"
      },
      {
        "id": "subtitle",
        "component": "body",
        "text": "Keep track of active, pending, and completed system integrations, compliances, and product enhancements."
      },
      {
        "id": "summary_stats",
        "component": "metric_row",
        "cols": 3,
        "metrics": [
          {
            "value": "3",
            "label": "Active",
            "accent": "#10b981"
          },
          {
            "value": "3",
            "label": "Pending",
            "accent": "#f59e0b"
          },
          {
            "value": "2",
            "label": "Completed",
            "accent": "#3b82f6"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "status_filters",
        "component": "chip_group",
        "label": "Filter by Status",
        "layout": "wrap",
        "chips": [
          {
            "label": "All (8)",
